<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Calculating disjoint probabilities and inverse cumulative temperatures for a uniform distribution</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>The daily high temperature (\(T\)) in Kisumu during July is <b>uniformly distributed</b> between <b>{@a@}\(^{\circ}\text{C}\)</b> and <b>{@b@}\(^{\circ}\text{C}\)</b>.</p>

<p><b>a) </b> Calculate the probability that on a randomly selected day, the high temperature is either <b>less than {@c@}\(^{\circ}\text{C}\)</b> OR <b>greater than {@d@}\(^{\circ}\text{C}\)</b>.</p>
<p><i>(Enter your answer as a fully simplified fraction).</i></p>
<p>\(P =\) [[input:ans1]]</p>
<div>[[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div>

<p><b>b) </b> A meteorologist states that the probability of the temperature being less than or equal to a specific unknown temperature \(t\) is exactly <b>\({@target_prob_tex@}\)</b>.</p>
<p>Use the cumulative distribution formula to find the exact temperature \(t\).</p>
<p>\(t =\) [[input:ans2]] \(^{\circ}\text{C}\)</p>
<div>[[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><b>Worked Solution:</b></p>

<p><b>Part a: Disjoint Probabilities</b><br>
The total width of our uniform distribution is \(b - a = {@b@} - {@a@} = {@w@}\).</p>
<p>Because the events "less than {@c@}" and "greater than {@d@}" do not overlap (they are mutually exclusive), we calculate their probabilities separately and add them together:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\( \displaystyle P(T < {@c@}) = \frac{{@c@} - {@a@}}{{@w@}} = \frac{{@c - a@}}{{@w@}} \)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\( \displaystyle P(T > {@d@}) = \frac{{@b@} - {@d@}}{{@w@}} = \frac{{@b - d@}}{{@w@}} \)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\( \displaystyle P(T < {@c@} \text{ or } T > {@d@}) = \frac{{@c - a@}}{{@w@}} + \frac{{@b - d@}}{{@w@}} = \frac{{@c - a + b - d@}}{{@w@}} \)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px; font-size: 1.2em;">\( \displaystyle \boxed{ P(\text{combined}) = {@ta1@} } \)</p>

<p><b>Part b: Inverse Cumulative Probability</b><br>
We are given the cumulative probability \(P(T \le t) = {@target_prob_tex@}\). For a uniform distribution, the formula for cumulative probability is:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\( \displaystyle P(T \le t) = \frac{t - a}{b - a} \)</p>
<p>Substitute the known values into the formula and solve for \(t\):</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\( \displaystyle \frac{t - {@a@}}{{@w@}} = {@target_prob_tex@} \)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\( \displaystyle t - {@a@} = {@target_prob_tex@} \times {@w@} \)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\( \displaystyle t - {@a@} = {@target_prob_num * w@} \)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px; font-size: 1.2em;">\( \displaystyle \boxed{ t = {@ta2@} } \)</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
